    "result": "Perfect! All tests pass. Here's a summary of the fixes:\n\n## Summary\n\nI fixed the two failing tests in the frai-core test suite:\n\n### 1. **Governance Test Fix** (`src/finetune/governance.test.js`)\n- **Issue**: The test imports `APPROVAL_STATUSES` as a named export, but it was only exported in the default export object\n- **Fix**: Added named exports at the top of `src/finetune/index.js` to re-export the constants from `schema.js`:\n  ```javascript\n  export {\n    APPROVAL_STATUSES,\n    DATA_SENSITIVITY_LEVELS,\n    DEFAULT_GOVERNANCE_TEMPLATE,\n    GOVERNANCE_SECTIONS,\n    RISK_LEVELS\n  };\n  ```\n\n### 2. **Eval Test Fix** (`src/eval/index.test.js`)\n- **Issue**: The `toxicityMetric` function was receiving the references array as the second parameter and treating it as banned terms, causing all outputs to be incorrectly flagged as toxic\n- **Fix**: Changed the `toxicityMetric` signature to only accept `outputs` and always use `defaultBannedTerms`, removing the problematic second parameter\n\n## Commands Run and Results\n\n```bash\n# Run tests - ALL 28 TESTS PASS \u2713\npnpm --filter frai-core test\n\n# Build - succeeds (no build step needed for ES modules)\npnpm --filter frai-core build\n```\n\nAll 28 tests pass across 8 test files. All public exports remain intact and functional.",
